VeridianOS: no unused variable/parameters without getutent_r() or innetgr()

musl provides neither getutent_r() nor innetgr(), and GCC reported:

- modules/pam_timestamp/pam_timestamp.c:231 "unused variable 'utbuf'"
  (check_login_time): the buffer is only passed to getutent_r(); it is now
  declared under the same HAVE_GETUTENT_R condition as that call.
- modules/pam_succeed_if/pam_succeed_if.c:266 and :279 "unused parameter"
  'host', 'user' and 'group' (evaluate_innetgr, evaluate_notinnetgr):
  they are only passed to innetgr(). The file already marks pamh with
  SOMETIMES_UNUSED (UNUSED when HAVE_INNETGR, since only the fallback logs
  through it); the three parameters get the mirror-image macro,
  UNUSED_WITHOUT_INNETGR (UNUSED when innetgr() is missing).

No behaviour change in either configuration.


diff -ru a/modules/pam_succeed_if/pam_succeed_if.c b/modules/pam_succeed_if/pam_succeed_if.c
--- a/modules/pam_succeed_if/pam_succeed_if.c	2026-10-08 17:20:38.592779853 -0400
+++ b/modules/pam_succeed_if/pam_succeed_if.c	2026-10-08 17:20:38.602781756 -0400
@@ -257,13 +257,18 @@
 
 #ifdef HAVE_INNETGR
 # define SOMETIMES_UNUSED UNUSED
+# define UNUSED_WITHOUT_INNETGR
 #else
 # define SOMETIMES_UNUSED
+# define UNUSED_WITHOUT_INNETGR UNUSED
 #endif
 
 /* Return PAM_SUCCESS if the (host,user) is in the netgroup. */
